WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.370 --> 00:00:03.220
- Now is your most recent album 15 years,

00:00:03.220 --> 00:00:04.870
after up So tell me about this album

00:00:04.870 --> 00:00:05.703
'cause you did

00:00:05.703 --> 00:00:07.150
this record all on your own.

00:00:07.150 --> 00:00:08.010
This isn't working

00:00:08.010 --> 00:00:09.060
with previous writers

00:00:09.060 --> 00:00:09.893
or producers you worked

00:00:09.893 --> 00:00:10.726
with this is you.

00:00:10.726 --> 00:00:11.950
- Yeah, I needed to do something

00:00:11.950 --> 00:00:13.340
that was really super independent

00:00:13.340 --> 00:00:14.640
musically and creatively

00:00:14.640 --> 00:00:15.537
and a song like life's

00:00:15.537 --> 00:00:19.010
about to get good.

00:00:19.010 --> 00:00:20.610
It's all about optimism

00:00:20.610 --> 00:00:22.820
and looking forward to what's next.

00:00:22.820 --> 00:00:25.430
And the whole thing was a reminder

00:00:25.430 --> 00:00:27.947
that I can do this on my own.

00:00:31.010 --> 00:00:32.970
After divorce you it's

00:00:32.970 --> 00:00:34.910
a server of so many things.

00:00:34.910 --> 00:00:36.390
And you have to find

00:00:36.390 --> 00:00:38.090
and rediscover your independence.

00:00:38.090 --> 00:00:38.923
- Yeah.

00:00:38.923 --> 00:00:39.756
- So this was an exercise

00:00:39.756 --> 00:00:42.348
of independence and I've really--

00:00:42.348 --> 00:00:43.200
- I've heard people go through that

00:00:43.200 --> 00:00:45.490
- It was great therapy.

00:00:45.490 --> 00:00:47.310
Well, and also because my ex husband

00:00:47.310 --> 00:00:48.540
was my producer,

00:00:48.540 --> 00:00:49.390
and my co-writer,

00:00:49.390 --> 00:00:52.130
so it was this huge Oh My Gosh!

00:00:52.130 --> 00:00:54.420
Every element of my life,

00:00:54.420 --> 00:00:56.290
parenting, songwriting,

00:00:56.290 --> 00:00:58.900
record-making, partnership,

00:00:58.900 --> 00:01:01.570
all of that had to,

00:01:01.570 --> 00:01:03.220
I was never alone

00:01:03.220 --> 00:01:04.053
in all of that.

00:01:05.180 --> 00:01:06.250
- I've never really thought about it

00:01:06.250 --> 00:01:07.083
but it's the server

00:01:07.083 --> 00:01:07.916
of a lot of ties.

00:01:07.916 --> 00:01:08.749
- A lot of things,

00:01:08.749 --> 00:01:09.800
so I had a lot of...

00:01:09.800 --> 00:01:11.810
and I'd lost my voice.

00:01:11.810 --> 00:01:14.040
I had to start over

00:01:14.040 --> 00:01:15.130
with my voice.

00:01:15.130 --> 00:01:16.930
- Did you like lose your voice physically

00:01:16.930 --> 00:01:18.800
or just everything mental emotional,

00:01:18.800 --> 00:01:21.090
everything kind of just felt like wow!

00:01:21.090 --> 00:01:22.270
- I got Lyme disease

00:01:22.270 --> 00:01:24.140
at the end of the up tour.

00:01:24.140 --> 00:01:25.490
The vocal cord nerves

00:01:25.490 --> 00:01:27.760
were damaged each side

00:01:27.760 --> 00:01:29.360
and I had to get

00:01:29.360 --> 00:01:31.080
an open throat surgery

00:01:31.080 --> 00:01:32.650
not like the cords are fine,

00:01:32.650 --> 00:01:33.483
- Okay,

00:01:33.483 --> 00:01:34.800
- but they just don't have

00:01:36.591 --> 00:01:39.460
the strings, the nerves are just weak.

00:01:39.460 --> 00:01:40.293
- Does not have

00:01:40.293 --> 00:01:41.126
the same elasticities,

00:01:41.126 --> 00:01:41.959
like the same flow.

00:01:41.959 --> 00:01:43.710
